                  "text": "Several AEC AI consultants publish credible case studies featuring quantified results, with Allsite.ai being a prominent example.\n\n**Allsite.ai** offers numerous case studies demonstrating tangible benefits through their AI-powered civil engineering design tools, Level AI and Service AI. Key quantified results from their projects include:\n*   A 100x speed increase in initial design processes.\n*   £2 million cost savings delivered on a single pilot project for a leading US house builder through automated 3D modeling from 2D layouts.\n*   A 60% reduction in overall process time.\n*   For the Wyoming Land Development project, Level AI and Service AI cut preliminary design hours by approximately 25% across a 60+ lot, 12-acre infill site.\n*   Inertia Engineering utilized Level AI and Service AI at Dawn West, Queensland, achieving earthworks balanced within 200 m³, which resulted in savings of approximately $2.5 million compared to the initial design surface.\n*   Brookfield and Wood Rodgers employed Level AI to grade a 400-acre California community, involving 1,500 lots, 23 detention ponds, and a 650,000-cubic-yard cut-fill balance across staged earthworks. Designs that typically took weeks were completed in days.\n*   Stantec used Level AI to compare six-warehouse layouts in Ontario, returning grading, retaining-wall, and earthworks quantities in less than a day per option.\n*   Civix completed servicing iterations for 210 Auckland lots in under an hour for the Selo Land Development project.\n\nWhile other firms like YegaTech offer case studies that highlight \"Real Firms, Real Outcomes\" and provide client testimonials, the initial search results for YegaTech's published case studies generally present more qualitative benefits such as improving data quality, establishing a repeatable innovation process, or moving from AI apprehension to a firm-wide strategy. They also discuss their own experiences in developing AI solutions with associated costs and timeframes."
